# Component Development Patterns

## Component Structure
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Add `'use client'` directive for client components
- Export as default with proper naming
- Use proper prop interfaces extending React.HTMLAttributes

## UI Component Standards
- All UI components in [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/)
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Support dark mode with `dark:` classes
- Include proper accessibility attributes
- Use Lucide React icons consistently

## Layout Components
- Header: [src/components/layout/Header.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/Header.tsx)
- Navigation: [src/components/layout/HorizontalNav.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/HorizontalNav.tsx)
- Conditional Layout: [src/components/layout/ConditionalLayout.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/ConditionalLayout.tsx)

## Form Components
- Use React Hook Form with Zod validation
- Include proper error handling and display
- Support loading states
- Use consistent form field patterns

## Modal and Dialog Components
- Use Modal component for overlays
- Include proper focus management
- Support keyboard navigation
- Use proper ARIA attributes

## State Management in Components
- Use local state for component-specific data
- Use Redux for global application state
- Use Context for authentication and theme
- Avoid prop drilling with proper state management

## Styling Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Support responsive design (mobile-first)
- Include dark mode support
- Use consistent spacing and typography
- Follow design system patterns

## Component Props
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces
- Include optional props with defaults
- Use proper event handlers
- Support className merging with cn() utility

## Error Handling
- Use ErrorBoundary for component errors
- Provide fallback UI for loading states
- Handle async operations properly
- Display user-friendly error messages

## Accessibility
- Use proper semantic HTML
- Include ARIA labels and roles
- Support keyboard navigation
- Ensure proper color contrast
- Use proper heading hierarchy